                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "975010f1-6109-30d3-a091-615966deceb1",
                                        "entry_id": "df68a255-8f13-30a8-9e49-77ebb71b45fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To form or emit foam."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4e8d5ab-a25a-415d-b044-0af9aa512576",
                                                "sense_id": "975010f1-6109-30d3-a091-615966deceb1",
                                                "text": "[…] And that is it\nHath made me rig my navy; at whose burthen\nThe anger'd ocean foams; with which I meant\nTo scourge the ingratitude that despiteful Rome\nCast on my noble father."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5404a59-cdd8-4f12-adcf-6455932a637c",
                                                "sense_id": "975010f1-6109-30d3-a091-615966deceb1",
                                                "text": "When the fierce North-wind with his airy forces\nRears up the Baltic to a foaming fury;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "036cd09b-5db1-43ff-873f-2bd3d63e2d9d",
                                                "sense_id": "975010f1-6109-30d3-a091-615966deceb1",
                                                "text": "They were both silent for a measure of moments, and then Syme's speech came with a rush, like the sudden foaming of champagne."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f88b9e8f-74b1-39ad-96c5-19cd354375e8",
                                        "entry_id": "df68a255-8f13-30a8-9e49-77ebb71b45fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To spew saliva as foam; to foam at the mouth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b07ff97e-b0c1-4ad8-8bc5-36238851079f",
                                                "sense_id": "f88b9e8f-74b1-39ad-96c5-19cd354375e8",
                                                "text": "[…] to London will we march amain,\nAnd once again bestride our foaming steeds,\nAnd once again cry ‘Charge upon our foes!’\nBut never once again turn back and fly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49076d59-56f5-4630-a3db-b425153b16e0",
                                                "sense_id": "f88b9e8f-74b1-39ad-96c5-19cd354375e8",
                                                "text": "Master, I have brought unto thee my son, which hath a dumb spirit; And wheresoever he taketh him, he teareth him: and he foameth, and gnasheth with his teeth, and pineth away."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c9fc07e-b9db-48e6-8b70-356df151f62e",
                                                "sense_id": "f88b9e8f-74b1-39ad-96c5-19cd354375e8",
                                                "text": "But I was talking to the wind; for whether my tears, my attitude, or the disorder of my dress prov'd fresh incentives, or whether he was not under the dominion of desires he could not bridle, but snorting and foaming with lust and rage, he renews his attack, seizes me, and again attempts to extend and fix me on the settee […]",
                                                "translation": "Fanny Hill",
                                                "english": "Fanny Hill"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e9505e4-1249-3c84-a1d0-5201ac42b823",
                                        "entry_id": "df68a255-8f13-30a8-9e49-77ebb71b45fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To coat or cover with foam."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee62e8c9-3bf4-488c-8984-e183f570d81d",
                                                "sense_id": "9e9505e4-1249-3c84-a1d0-5201ac42b823",
                                                "text": "It used to be common practice to foam the runway prior to an emergency landing, in case a fuel-fed fire occurred."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
